# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use dry-run jobs to get the usage in resource units and service-side validation a job would incur on a real QPU without spending QPU time."
msgstr "Gunakan job dry-run untuk mendapatkan penggunaan dalam unit sumber dan pengesahan sebelah perkhidmatan yang akan dikenakan oleh sesuatu job pada QPU sebenar tanpa menghabiskan masa QPU."

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dry-run jobs"
msgstr "Job dry-run"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dry-run jobs {#dry-run-jobs}"
msgstr "Job dry-run {#dry-run-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A dry-run job runs your workload through IBM Quantum&reg; Compute Service without using any QPU time. Use a dry-run job to do the following before you commit to a real run:\n"
msgstr "Job dry-run menjalankan beban kerja anda melalui IBM Quantum&reg; Compute Service tanpa menggunakan sebarang masa QPU. Gunakan job dry-run untuk melakukan perkara berikut sebelum anda membuat larian sebenar:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Get the usage that the job would incur on the real QPU.\n"
msgstr "**Dapatkan penggunaan yang akan dikenakan oleh job pada QPU sebenar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Validate the job.** Quantum Compute checks the job's parameters, the same way it does for a real job.\n"
msgstr "**Sahkan job.** Quantum Compute menyemak parameter job, sama seperti untuk job sebenar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Get the [circuit timing schedule](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing)**, if you request it, to debug the job before you run it for real.\n"
msgstr "**Dapatkan [jadual masa litar](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing)**, jika anda memintanya, untuk menyahpepijat job sebelum anda menjalankannya secara sebenar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unlike dry-run jobs, local testing (fake backends and [Qiskit Aer](/guides/simulate-with-qiskit-aer)) runs on your own machine and therefore cannot provide usage numbers, service-side validation, or service timing information. To compare the two approaches, see [Mock devices compared to fake backends](#mock-vs-fake).\n"
msgstr "Tidak seperti job dry-run, pengujian tempatan (fake backend dan [Qiskit Aer](/guides/simulate-with-qiskit-aer)) berjalan pada mesin anda sendiri dan oleh itu tidak dapat menyediakan angka penggunaan, pengesahan sebelah perkhidmatan, atau maklumat masa perkhidmatan. Untuk membandingkan kedua-dua pendekatan, lihat [Peranti mock berbanding fake backend](#mock-vs-fake).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"- `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.51.0 or later is required for dry-run jobs.\n"
"- Dry-run jobs are available in all regions, and are only available on the Flex, Premium, and On-Prem plans. They are not available on the Open or Pay-As-You-Go plans.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"- `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.51.0 atau lebih baharu diperlukan untuk job dry-run.\n"
"- Job dry-run tersedia di semua wilayah, dan hanya tersedia pada pelan Flex, Premium dan On-Prem. Ia tidak tersedia pada pelan Open atau Pay-As-You-Go.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "How it works {#how-it-works}"
msgstr "Cara ia berfungsi {#how-it-works}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To run a dry-run job, pass `dry_run=True` to the primitive's `run()` method:\n"
msgstr "Untuk menjalankan job dry-run, hantarkan `dry_run=True` kepada kaedah `run()` primitif:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`dry_run` is an argument of the `run()` method (the default is `False`), not a runtime option. It is available to all primitives.\n"
msgstr "`dry_run` ialah argumen bagi kaedah `run()` (nilai lalai ialah `False`), bukan pilihan runtime. Ia tersedia untuk semua primitif.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A dry-run job has the following characteristics:\n"
msgstr "Job dry-run mempunyai ciri-ciri berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "It runs in IBM Quantum Compute Service in the cloud, not on your machine.\n"
msgstr "Ia berjalan dalam IBM Quantum Compute Service di awan, bukan pada mesin anda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "It uses the calibration data from the real QPU, not just a snapshot. \n"
msgstr "Ia menggunakan data penentukuran daripada QPU sebenar, bukan sekadar syot kilat. \n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Its results keep the expected schema and follow the expected shape of results from the real QPU, but contain randomized mock data. They are not actual or simulated measurement results, so do not use them to check physical correctness.\n"
msgstr "Keputusannya mengekalkan skema yang dijangka dan mengikut bentuk keputusan yang dijangka daripada QPU sebenar, tetapi mengandungi data mock rawak. Ia bukan keputusan pengukuran sebenar atau simulasi, jadi jangan gunakannya untuk menyemak ketepatan fizikal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Processing happens on the server, so the job might not finish immediately.\n"
msgstr "Pemprosesan berlaku pada pelayan, jadi job mungkin tidak selesai serta-merta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuit size, shots, and other limits are the same as for any job of that program.\n"
msgstr "Saiz litar, shot dan had lain adalah sama seperti untuk mana-mana job bagi program tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`dry_run=True` also works when the backend is already a mock device.\n"
msgstr "`dry_run=True` juga berfungsi apabila backend sudah pun peranti mock.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the usage {#read-the-usage}"
msgstr "Baca penggunaan {#read-the-usage}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The usage of a completed dry-run job is the usage the same job would incur on the real QPU, except in rare situations where calibration data changes significantly after the dry-run job and before the job on a real QPU.\n"
msgstr "Penggunaan job dry-run yang telah selesai ialah penggunaan yang akan dikenakan oleh job yang sama pada QPU sebenar, kecuali dalam situasi jarang apabila data penentukuran berubah dengan ketara selepas job dry-run dan sebelum job pada QPU sebenar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.usage()` returns the usage in seconds.\n"
msgstr "`job.usage()` mengembalikan penggunaan dalam saat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.metrics()[\"usage\"]` returns the same data together with the usage status.\n"
msgstr "`job.metrics()[\"usage\"]` mengembalikan data yang sama bersama status penggunaan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dry-run usage is not charged, does not consume your plan allocation, and does not count against any limits.\n"
msgstr "Penggunaan dry-run tidak dicaj, tidak menggunakan peruntukan pelan anda, dan tidak dikira terhadap sebarang had.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Do not use job.usage_estimation with dry-run jobs\">\n"
"Do not use `job.usage_estimation` on a dry-run job. Use `job.usage()`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Jangan gunakan job.usage_estimation dengan job dry-run\">\n"
"Jangan gunakan `job.usage_estimation` pada job dry-run. Gunakan `job.usage()`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.usage()` returns `0` until the usage calculation is final, so wait for the job to finish before you read it.\n"
msgstr "`job.usage()` mengembalikan `0` sehingga pengiraan penggunaan dimuktamadkan, jadi tunggu job selesai sebelum anda membacanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuit timing schedule {#circuit-timing-schedule}"
msgstr "Jadual masa litar {#circuit-timing-schedule}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To request the circuit timing schedule, use the same option as for a real job. For full details, see [Visualize circuit timing](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing).\n"
msgstr "Untuk meminta jadual masa litar, gunakan pilihan yang sama seperti untuk job sebenar. Untuk butiran penuh, lihat [Visualisasikan masa litar](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Limitations {#limitations}"
msgstr "Batasan {#limitations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Job and batch modes only.** Dry-run jobs can only run in [job mode](/guides/execution-modes#job-mode) and [batch mode](/guides/execution-modes#batch-mode).\n"
msgstr "**Mod job dan batch sahaja.** Job dry-run hanya boleh dijalankan dalam [job mode](/guides/execution-modes#job-mode) dan [batch mode](/guides/execution-modes#batch-mode).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Flex, Premium, and On-Prem plans only.** Dry-run jobs are not available on the Open or Pay-As-You-Go plans.\n"
msgstr "**Pelan Flex, Premium dan On-Prem sahaja.** Job dry-run tidak tersedia pada pelan Open atau Pay-As-You-Go.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mock devices {#mock-devices}"
msgstr "Peranti mock {#mock-devices}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mock devices are the implementation behind dry-run jobs. Dry-run jobs hide mock devices by default, but you encounter them in these cases:\n"
msgstr "Peranti mock ialah pelaksanaan di sebalik job dry-run. Job dry-run menyembunyikan peranti mock secara lalai, tetapi anda akan menemuinya dalam kes berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Instances configured to access only mock devices.** Example: if you use `service.backend(\"ibm_phoenix\")` to submit a dry-run job on `ibm_phoenix`, but your instance doesn't have access to `ibm_phoenix`,  you will get a `QiskitBackendNotFoundError`. Instead, select the mock device directly with `service.backend(\"mock_phoenix\")`.\n"
msgstr "**Instance yang dikonfigurasikan untuk mengakses peranti mock sahaja.** Contoh: jika anda menggunakan `service.backend(\"ibm_phoenix\")` untuk menghantar job dry-run pada `ibm_phoenix`, tetapi instance anda tidak mempunyai akses kepada `ibm_phoenix`,  anda akan mendapat `QiskitBackendNotFoundError`. Sebaliknya, pilih peranti mock secara terus dengan `service.backend(\"mock_phoenix\")`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Compute resources.** Mock devices are hidden by default on the [Compute resources](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) page. The table on the page has a filter option to include them, but only the Flex, Premium, and On-Prem plans have access to mock devices.\n"
msgstr "**Sumber pengkomputeran.** Peranti mock disembunyikan secara lalai pada halaman [Compute resources](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers). Jadual pada halaman itu mempunyai pilihan penapis untuk memasukkannya, tetapi hanya pelan Flex, Premium dan On-Prem yang mempunyai akses kepada peranti mock.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Workloads table.** Jobs from mock devices are hidden by default on the [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) page. The table has a filter option (the funnel icon) to display them.\n"
msgstr "**Jadual beban kerja.** Job daripada peranti mock disembunyikan secara lalai pada halaman [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads). Jadual itu mempunyai pilihan penapis (ikon corong) untuk memaparkannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Python API.** `service.backends()` and `service.jobs()` exclude mock devices unless you call them with `include_mocks=True`. `IBMBackend.is_mock` indicates whether a backend is a mock device. `service.least_busy()` never returns a mock device.\n"
msgstr "**API Python.** `service.backends()` dan `service.jobs()` mengecualikan peranti mock melainkan anda memanggilnya dengan `include_mocks=True`. `IBMBackend.is_mock` menunjukkan sama ada sesuatu backend ialah peranti mock. `service.least_busy()` tidak pernah mengembalikan peranti mock.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"mock-vs-fake\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mock devices compared to fake backends {#mock-devices-compared-to-fake-backends}"
msgstr "Peranti mock berbanding fake backend {#mock-devices-compared-to-fake-backends}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The names are similar, but a mock device and a [fake backend](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider) are different things. A fake backend is a local object in your Python environment. A mock device is a cloud resource in IBM Quantum Compute Service.\n"
msgstr "Namanya serupa, tetapi peranti mock dan [fake backend](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider) ialah dua perkara yang berbeza. Fake backend ialah objek tempatan dalam persekitaran Python anda. Peranti mock ialah sumber awan dalam IBM Quantum Compute Service.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | Mock device (for example `mock_phoenix`) | Fake backend (for example `FakeManilaV2`) |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| What it is | A device in IBM Quantum Compute Service | A Python class in `qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider` |\n"
"| Where it runs | Cloud, in the service | Locally, on your machine |\n"
"| How you get it | `service.backend(\"mock_phoenix\")`, or automatically with `run(..., dry_run=True)` | `from qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider import ...` |\n"
"| Account and instance | Specific plans only (Flex, Premium, or On-Prem) | All instances and plans |\n"
"| Calibration | Live, matches the real device at any time | Fixed snapshot shipped with the installed package |\n"
"| Results | Randomized data with the expected schema. Not a simulation | Noisy simulation that uses the snapshot's noise model |\n"
"| Physically meaningful results | No. Never use them to check correctness | Approximately, within the limits of the noise model |\n"
"| Usage reported | Yes | None |\n"
"| Charged or counted against plan allocation or limits | No | No |\n"
"| Job validation | Done by the service, same as a real job | Limited to what the client checks |\n"
"| Timing schedule | Available on request  | Not available |\n"
"| Execution modes | Job and batch mode only. Sessions are blocked | Session syntax accepted but ignored (local mode has no real sessions or batches) |\n"
"| Completion | Asynchronous, on the server | Runs locally and returns when finished |\n"
"| Shown in platform interface and API lists | Hidden by default (Compute resources, Workloads table, `backends()`, `jobs()`). Opt in to show | Never, because nothing is sent to the service |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | Peranti mock (contohnya `mock_phoenix`) | Fake backend (contohnya `FakeManilaV2`) |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| Apa itu | Peranti dalam IBM Quantum Compute Service | Kelas Python dalam `qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider` |\n"
"| Tempat ia berjalan | Awan, dalam perkhidmatan | Secara tempatan, pada mesin anda |\n"
"| Cara mendapatkannya | `service.backend(\"mock_phoenix\")`, atau secara automatik dengan `run(..., dry_run=True)` | `from qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider import ...` |\n"
"| Akaun dan instance | Pelan tertentu sahaja (Flex, Premium atau On-Prem) | Semua instance dan pelan |\n"
"| Penentukuran | Langsung, sepadan dengan peranti sebenar pada bila-bila masa | Syot kilat tetap yang disertakan bersama pakej yang dipasang |\n"
"| Keputusan | Data rawak dengan skema yang dijangka. Bukan simulasi | Simulasi berhingar yang menggunakan model hingar syot kilat |\n"
"| Keputusan bermakna secara fizikal | Tidak. Jangan sekali-kali gunakannya untuk menyemak ketepatan | Secara anggaran, dalam had model hingar |\n"
"| Penggunaan dilaporkan | Ya | Tiada |\n"
"| Dicaj atau dikira terhadap peruntukan pelan atau had | Tidak | Tidak |\n"
"| Pengesahan job | Dilakukan oleh perkhidmatan, sama seperti job sebenar | Terhad kepada apa yang disemak oleh klien |\n"
"| Jadual masa | Tersedia atas permintaan  | Tidak tersedia |\n"
"| Mod pelaksanaan | Job dan batch mode sahaja. Session disekat | Sintaks session diterima tetapi diabaikan (mod tempatan tiada session atau batch sebenar) |\n"
"| Penyiapan | Tak segerak, pada pelayan | Berjalan secara tempatan dan mengembalikan hasil apabila selesai |\n"
"| Dipaparkan dalam antara muka platform dan senarai API | Disembunyikan secara lalai (Compute resources, jadual Workloads, `backends()`, `jobs()`). Pilih untuk memaparkan | Tidak pernah, kerana tiada apa dihantar kepada perkhidmatan |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to choose {#how-to-choose}"
msgstr "Cara memilih {#how-to-choose}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To find out **how much usage the job will consume, or whether the service will accept it**, use a dry-run job.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengetahui **berapa banyak penggunaan yang akan digunakan oleh job, atau sama ada perkhidmatan akan menerimanya**, gunakan job dry-run.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To find out **what the output might look like**, or to work offline, use a fake backend or Aer.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengetahui **rupa output yang mungkin**, atau untuk bekerja luar talian, gunakan fake backend atau Aer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To do both, iterate on circuits and results with a fake backend, then dry-run as the last check before the real QPU.\n"
msgstr "Untuk melakukan kedua-duanya, lelaran pada litar dan keputusan dengan fake backend, kemudian jalankan dry-run sebagai semakan terakhir sebelum QPU sebenar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Common points of confusion {#common-points-of-confusion}"
msgstr "Perkara yang sering mengelirukan {#common-points-of-confusion}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A mock device is not a simulator.** Its output is random, so sampling a Bell circuit on `mock_phoenix` does not return a Bell distribution. If you want realistic noisy output, use a fake backend.\n"
msgstr "**Peranti mock bukan simulator.** Outputnya rawak, jadi pensampelan litar Bell pada `mock_phoenix` tidak mengembalikan taburan Bell. Jika anda mahukan output berhingar yang realistik, gunakan fake backend.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A fake backend is not the live device.** Its calibration is a snapshot and might be out of date. A mock device tracks the real calibration, so transpiled circuits and timing match what the QPU sees today.\n"
msgstr "**Fake backend bukan peranti langsung.** Penentukurannya ialah syot kilat dan mungkin sudah lapuk. Peranti mock menjejaki penentukuran sebenar, jadi litar yang ditranspilasi dan masa sepadan dengan apa yang QPU lihat hari ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Neither runs on real hardware.** Neither consumes QPU time, but only a dry-run job goes through the service.\n"
msgstr "**Kedua-duanya tidak berjalan pada perkakasan sebenar.** Kedua-duanya tidak menggunakan masa QPU, tetapi hanya job dry-run yang melalui perkhidmatan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`usage_estimation` is not the dry-run estimate.** For a dry-run job, `job.usage()` returns the seconds of usage your job would be charged on a real QPU.\n"
msgstr "**`usage_estimation` bukan anggaran dry-run.** Bagi job dry-run, `job.usage()` mengembalikan saat penggunaan yang akan dicaj untuk job anda pada QPU sebenar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use cases {#use-cases}"
msgstr "Kes penggunaan {#use-cases}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Students and courses {#students-and-courses}"
msgstr "Pelajar dan kursus {#students-and-courses}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An administrator restricts an instance to mock devices only, using the QPU customization toggle when [creating or editing the instance](/guides/instances#add-instance). Students then validate their payloads end-to-end without consuming real QPU time or RUs. Because the instance has access only to mock devices, students select the backend by its mock name:\n"
msgstr "Seorang pentadbir menghadkan instance kepada peranti mock sahaja, menggunakan togol penyesuaian QPU semasa [mencipta atau mengedit instance](/guides/instances#add-instance). Pelajar kemudian mengesahkan payload mereka dari hujung ke hujung tanpa menggunakan masa QPU sebenar atau RU. Oleh sebab instance hanya mempunyai akses kepada peranti mock, pelajar memilih backend mengikut nama mock-nya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Project planning {#project-planning}"
msgstr "Perancangan projek {#project-planning}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A team about to start a project dry-runs representative jobs to see the RUs the project needs, before choosing a plan or allocation:\n"
msgstr "Sebuah pasukan yang hampir memulakan projek menjalankan dry-run job yang mewakili untuk melihat RU yang diperlukan projek, sebelum memilih pelan atau peruntukan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Final check before running on a real QPU {#final-check-before-running-on-a-real-qpu}"
msgstr "Semakan akhir sebelum menjalankan pada QPU sebenar {#final-check-before-running-on-a-real-qpu}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Validate parameters and inspect the timing schedule with `dry_run=True`, then drop the argument and run on the real QPU. Nothing else in your code changes:\n"
